{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Group 3 was one of six groups of national teams competing in the group stage of the [[1982 FIFA World Cup]]. Play began on 13 June with the opening match of the tournament and ended on 23 June 1982.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/82full.html |title=World Cup 1982 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The group consisted of four teams: The seeded team, the reigning world champions [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]], [[Belgium national football team|Belgium]], [[Hungary national football team|Hungary]] and [[El Salvador national football team|El Salvador]].

Belgium won the group and advanced to the second round, along with Argentina. Despite recording [[Hungary v El Salvador (1982 FIFA World Cup)|the biggest victory in World Cup history]], Hungary failed to advance.

